 "text": "The man who named the Big Bang didn't even believe in it. 1927, Belgium. Georges Lemaitre, a Catholic priest and physicist, has a wild idea. The universe is expanding, and it all began from one tiny point. Einstein reportedly told him, Your math is correct, but your physics is abominable. In 1949, astronomer Fred Hoyle, who thinks the universe has no beginning, calls it on BBC Radio, this Big Bang idea. The name sticks. In 1965, two American scientists detect faint leftover heat from the early universe. Le Maître hears the news shortly before he dies. A priest's idea, named by its biggest doubter. Every legend has a beginning.",
